MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_001: Ah, there's Talimun...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_002: Then we will move forward with the contracted work\nas scheduled. Thank you.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_003: He's with Ursula again...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_004: Someone was just there... From the glimpse I caught,\nit looked like Fianna.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_005: Haaah... Haaah... Why did I run? What was\nI thinking?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_006: Whew... There you are... Can we chat?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_007: U-Ursula! What can I do for you?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_008: I wanted to give you a proper thank-you for your\nhelp the other day.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_009: That poetry collection you selected for those\nhighborn buyers was well received.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_010: Talimun was pleased with the range and quality of\nthe poems, and that it wasn't all well-known poets.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_011: I find it difficult to judge artwork meant to appeal\nto the emotions, so your feedback was valuable.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_012: I only chose the poetry that spoke to my heart.\nNothing more.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_013: I picked verses on peace that filled me with longing\nand the tragic works that brought me serenity.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_014: Serenity? In tragedy?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_015: Yes. At first I'd find myself overwhelmed by grief\nand sadness, to the point I was moved to tears...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_016: But then I'd pray for those suffering people—and by\npraying for their serenity, I would find my own.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_017: Ah... I see...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_018: Since I lost my memory and can remember nothing\nof my past, I'm often afflicted by moments of anxiety.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_019: In those moments, I pray, and that helps me find\nsome peace... It's the same with those poems...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_020: Hm... I'm afraid I'm not making much sense...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_021: No, no. That sort of thing is just completely foreign\nto me.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_022: But I can tell your faith is a kind one, and sincere.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_023: You care about others, feel their pain as your own,\nand pray for them... Not everyone can say the same.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_024: I am not kind... Even just now, when you were\nspeaking to Talimu— I, um, never mind...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_025: What was that, Fianna?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_C_026: Oh, nothing. It was nothing.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_001: Please keep Talimun happy... Please keep\nTalimun safe...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_002: Here to pray again, Fianna? You're very diligent with\nyour practice.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_003: Oh, Ursula... Are you here to pray as well?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_004: No, prayer is not an act of faith I indulge in.\nI don't see any purpose myself.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_005: Oh... Really? May I ask why that is?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_006: My entire family was murdered, persecuted for the\nbloodmark they bore.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_007: My parents put their faith in the Church of Seiros,\nthe primary religion in Fódlan.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_008: When they knew they were going to die, they prayed\nto their goddess, believing they would be saved.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_009: I was the only one who escaped alive.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_010: Their faith did not save them. And ever since, prayer\nhas felt empty, and religious practice repels me.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_011: Oh...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_012: I'm sorry. I didn't mean to burden you with that.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_013: No, that's not it. I'm upset at myself for how\ninsensitive I've been...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_014: I had no idea you had suffered so.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_015: I imagined you as calm and content inside,\nconfident in Talimun's trust in you.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_016: Not many know the details of my past.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_017: But regardless of how I may feel, I don't criticize\nothers for their beliefs.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_018: You said you feel repelled... Are you not repelled\nwhen I pray in front of you?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_019: No, not at all. Because I believe there is kindness\nbehind your faith.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_020: I respect your beliefs, Fianna. You care for others\neven when you yourself are hurting.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_021: No, no... I'm not the caring person you think I am!
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_022: I've been envious of you and how close you are\nto Talimun!
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_023: And not once did I stop to think about you or\nhow you felt!
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_024: I don't blame you for your feelings, Fianna.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_025: *gasp*
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_026: Just try to relax. Can I bring you some water?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_027: Hnng... I'm sorry to be such a terrible inconvenience.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_028: It's no trouble at all. Really.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_B_029: {SetColor=Gray}To think she torments herself so...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_001: ...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_002: Ursula? Are you...praying?!
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_003: I am. It isn't going well. But I wanted to give your\napproach a try.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_004: My approach?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_005: With how I've been acting, I needed to make a\nchange, but...perhaps I ought to apologize directly.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_006: Apologize? To me? After the trouble I've caused you,\nsurely it should be me apologizing...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_007: Before, you said you were jealous of my presence\nat Talimun's side...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_008: The truth is I've been jealous of you too.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_009: But you still assigned me tasks. You trusted me with\nwork and spoke to me as you would anyone else.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_010: Talimun asked those things of me. I don't question\nhis judgment in such matters.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_011: He is concerned about your condition, and he\nappreciates the difficulty you must be facing.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_012: It has taken me...unerring excellence to attract his\nattentions, but when your name is mentioned...
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_013: Ah!
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_014: I was jealous of you. Jealous that mere mention of\nyour name would turn Talimun's head.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_015: It was cruel of me, knowing how you were suffering\nall the while.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_016: I was not always kind to you in my heart.\nI'm sorry for that.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_017: So that's why you were praying? Because you think\nI do it out of kindness?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_018: I thought it might help me understand what you\nmeant about finding peace. But it was no use.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_019: I can't do it. My prayers are empty.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_020: I see... Then there's something I can do for you.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_021: Let me pray... And may my prayers bring peace\nto your heart.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_022: You don't think I'm a hypocrite?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_023: I think you are kind. And I know you mean well.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_024: I will say, however... I am surprised to learn even\nsomeone as perfect as you can still be jealous.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_025: I can. To be honest, I would have Talimun all to\nmyself if I could.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_026: I can relate. I think we may have more in common\nthan we first thought, hm?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_027: I have no intention of setting my feelings aside, but\nI may find myself cheering you on before the end.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_028: Oh? And will that be...alright?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_029: Hehehe. Ursula, it was you who judged me to have\na kind heart, was it not?
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_030: In the spirit of that kindness, I'd be happy to dispose\nof any additional competition. Just say the word.
MID_SE_Urs_Fia_A_031: That...won't be necessary. Perhaps understanding\nyou will be more difficult than I imagined...